📊 Student Result Analysis using Python & Pandas
Overview

This project is a simple student result analysis built using Python, Pandas, and NumPy.
The goal of this project was to practice data analysis by working with a real dataset and
applying common Pandas operations to extract useful information.

The analysis includes finding toppers, calculating percentages, identifying students who passed
or failed, generating subject-wise statistics, and creating a cleaned dataset for further use.

Dataset

The dataset contains marks of 1000 students in the following subjects:

Hindi
English
Science
Mathematics
History
Geography

It also includes the total marks and other student-related information.

Features

The project performs the following analyses:

Find the highest scoring student.
Find the lowest scoring student.
Find the highest marks in each subject.
Find the student who scored the highest in each subject.
Find the lowest marks in each subject.
Find the student who scored the lowest in each subject.
Calculate each student's percentage.
Identify students who passed all subjects.
Identify students who failed based on subject marks or total marks.
Find students who achieved distinction.
Generate subject-wise statistics (highest, lowest, and average marks).
Calculate the overall pass percentage.
Calculate the overall fail percentage.
Display the top 10 students based on percentage.
Display the bottom 10 students based on percentage.
List students scoring above 80%.
List students scoring below 40%.
Export the processed dataset to a new CSV file.
